    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a> the Qing garrison in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> surrendered under the Three Point Agreement, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thubten-gyatso">13th Dalai Lama</a> declared that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>'s relationship with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> had ended, though almost no country formally recognised its independence.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simla-convention">Simla Convention</a> of 1913–1914 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> was rejected by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, but it defined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mcmahon-line">McMahon Line</a> between Tibet and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</li><li>In October 1950 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-liberation-army">People's Liberation Army</a> entered Chamdo, and in 1951 the Seventeen Point Agreement affirmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> created its own postal service in 1912 and printed its first postage stamps in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> that year, marked &quot;Tibet Government&quot; in Tibetan and &quot;Tibet&quot; in English.</p></aside>
    </section>

